othello -- Othello (Reversi)============================    othelloPlay Othello against the computer or another person on an 8x8 board.Players take turns placing a disk so that it flanks a line of theopponent's disks between the new disk and one already yours; everyopponent disk so trapped flips to your colour.  You must move when youcan.  When the board fills or neither side can move, the most disks wins.At the start it asks how many human players (0, 1 or 2) and, for a gameagainst the computer, a level from 1 (easy) to 5 (tough).  A move is twokeystrokes: the row letter A-H then the column number 1-8.  `Q' quits.Don Dodson's Othello, posted to comp.sources.games; freely used anddistributed.  Originals in SRC/othello3/ORIG.OS-9 note: the BSD bits it leaned on are replaced -- rand()/srand() forrandom()/srandom(), a plain read for the ioctl() keypoll it used only tostir the RNG, signal() for sigvec(), and usleep() from the shared library.